From: PowerPhone research platform <powerphone@csr460.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Amortize D5 FastMixer FMQ round trips over five native quanta

The FMQ192 candidate selected FastMixer as intended. One real hardware run
stopped during active playback after2.334 seconds; a fresh repeat sustained
the full7.85-second active interval with zero measured phase/dropout events
and no HAL errors through the quiet tail. The first error in the failed run
was lost to the log storm, so its exact cause is not established.

Use FMQ960/5 ms to reduce command/reply frequency fivefold while retaining
HAL960 < normal3840 and therefore the same existing static FastMixer.
Every FMQ still submits blocking192-frame native writes into the unchanged
192x20/full3840 ALSA ring. Keep the cross-call accepted-frame startup
counter, positional stereo, flagsNONE, and terminal active EPIPE checks.
This is a direct-hardware candidate, not a claim of qualification.
Capture remains unchanged.

--- a/audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp
@@ -76,9 +76,10 @@
 constexpr size_t kPlaybackAlsaBufferFrames = 3840;
 constexpr size_t kPlaybackAlsaStartThresholdFrames = kPlaybackAlsaBufferFrames;
 constexpr size_t kCaptureFrameworkBufferFrames = 1920;
-// A 1 ms HAL burst selects AudioFlinger's existing static FastMixer beneath
-// its 20 ms normal mixer. The independent physical ring remains 20 ms.
-constexpr size_t kPlaybackFrameworkBufferFrames = kPlaybackAlsaPeriodFrames;
+// A 5 ms HAL burst still selects the existing static FastMixer beneath the
+// 20 ms normal mixer, with fivefold fewer command/reply round trips than 1 ms.
+// The independent physical ring remains 20 ms with native 1 ms PCM writes.
+constexpr size_t kPlaybackFrameworkBufferFrames = 5 * kPlaybackAlsaPeriodFrames;
 constexpr uint32_t kPlaybackSecondWriteEfaultRetries = 32;
 constexpr uint32_t kPlaybackSecondWriteEfaultRetrySleepUs = 1000;
 constexpr int kPlaybackRtPriority = 90;
@@ -1758,8 +1759,8 @@
                 std::min(kPlaybackAlsaPeriodFrames, frameCount - transferredFrames);
         auto* chunk = static_cast<uint8_t*>(buffer) + transferredFrames * mFrameSizeBytes;
         const bool oversized = chunkFrames > std::numeric_limits<uint32_t>::max();
-        // Count accepted frames across FMQ calls: FastMixer submits one
-        // quantum per call, so a call-local offset cannot identify WRITEI #2.
+        // Count accepted frames across FMQ calls: valid bursts can be one
+        // quantum, so a call-local offset cannot always identify WRITEI #2.
         const size_t startupAcceptedFrames =
                 mPlaybackStartupAcceptedFrames.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
         const bool retryStartupSecondWrite =
@@ -1927,9 +1928,9 @@
         return ndk::ScopedAStatus::ok();
     }
     if (sampleRateHz == kRate && exactOutput) {
-        // HAL 1 ms < normal mixer 20 ms selects the existing static FastMixer
+        // HAL 5 ms < normal mixer 20 ms selects the existing static FastMixer
         // without a FAST output flag. It paces active audio and idle silence
-        // through blocking 192-frame writes, independently of the unchanged
+        // through five blocking 192-frame writes per FMQ, independently of the
         // 192x20 ALSA ring and its full 3,840-frame startup threshold.
         *bufferSizeFrames = kPlaybackFrameworkBufferFrames;
         return ndk::ScopedAStatus::ok();

